  "description": "Services converted to the dependency-injection pattern (SWLOR.Game.Server/Readmes/DependencyInjection.md). Each is an instance class <name>Service behind the interface I<name>Service, both in Domain.<domain>, registered in the container; static code reaches it through the property of the same name on SWLOR.Game.Server.Composition.GameServices. SWLOR.Architecture.Tests apply their rules to exactly these services: the pieces must exist, hold no static mutable state, keep the [NWNEventHandler] methods on an instance class of the service, and not be reached for by service location. The domain must match DomainMap.json. A service made of more than one class lists the others in an optional \"extras\" array (sorted by name), each an object with either a \"class\" (a further class of the service that static code reaches through its own GameServices property, named like its type) or a \"part\" (a class a large service is split into by responsibility). Either way the extra has its own instance class <Type>Service behind I<Type>Service in the same domain, registered in the container, and every rule applies to it too. Add a service here, sorted by name, in the pull request that converts it. There is no list of services in progress: a service is listed here only when it is fully converted.",
